1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,840
Some faces stay frozen in time.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,240
They were children when we first met them

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:06,796
on a Saturday morning

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,416
in a movie we wore out on VHS,

5
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,080
in a show the whole
family watched together.

6
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:13,996
And because they were children,

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,600
we assumed they had decades ahead of them.

8
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:20,440
Thirty-five young performers
never got those decades.

9
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:25,460
One of them died on the very same day
his television character died on screen.

10
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:29,980
One of them was taken by the person
who was supposed to protect her most.

11
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,980
One of them lent her voice
to characters you still quote today,

12
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,760
and most people never learned her name.

13
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:40,176
And one death on a front
doorstep in Los Angeles

14
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,460
changed American law forever.

15
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:47,416
Stay until the end because the last
name on this list happened recently,

16
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,776
and chances are,

17
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:52,360
you watched her grow up without
ever realizing she was gone.

18
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:55,976
Let's begin with a voice that
lived inside your childhood,

19
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,760
whether you knew it or not.

20
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,956
Judith Barsi was only ten years old.

21
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:04,416
She was the voice of Ducky
in The Land Before Time,

22
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,276
the little "yep, yep, yep"

23
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,416
that millions of kids repeated,

24
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,376
and Anne-Marie in All Dogs Go to Heaven.

25
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,276
In July of nineteen eighty-eight,

26
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:17,760
her father shot Judith and her mother
before turning the gun on himself.

27
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,900
Both of her films were
released after her death.

28
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:23,660
She never saw how loved they became.

29
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:26,836
River Phoenix was the face of a generation

30
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:30,436
from Stand by Me to My Own Private Idaho.

31
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:33,476
On Halloween night nineteen ninety-three,

32
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:37,000
he collapsed outside
The Viper Room in Los Angeles,

33
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:40,240
a lethal combination
of drugs in his system.

34
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,096
He was twenty-three.

35
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:45,520
His younger brother Joaquin
made the nine one one call.

36
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:50,020
Hollywood lost the actor many believed
would define the next thirty years.

37
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:54,156
Anton Yelchin played Chekov
in the rebooted Star Trek films

38
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:57,160
and carried indie movies
with a quiet brilliance.

39
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,296
In June two thousand sixteen,

40
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:03,640
his own Jeep rolled down his driveway
and pinned him against a gate.

41
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,236
He was twenty-seven,

42
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:09,100
and the accident led to a recall
of over a million vehicles.

43
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,716
Cameron Boyce

44
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,360
grew up in front of us.

45
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:14,576
Luke on Disney's Jessie,

46
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:16,460
Carlos in Descendants.

47
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,716
Off-screen,

48
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,820
he raised money and awareness
for causes most adults never touch.

49
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,016
In July two thousand nineteen,

50
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:27,120
he died in his sleep
from an epileptic seizure.

51
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,556
He was twenty,

52
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,440
and his family turned grief
into a foundation in his name.

53
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,320
Remember Froggy from The Little Rascals?

54
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:36,516
The raspy voice,

55
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,860
the spectacles?

56
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,780
That was Billy Laughlin.

57
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,396
After the shorts ended,

58
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:45,420
he stepped away from Hollywood
and lived like a regular kid.

59
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,049
In nineteen forty-eight,

60
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:48,549
at just sixteen,

61
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:52,313
he was killed when a truck struck
the motor scooter he was riding.

62
00:02:52,573 --> 00:02:55,633
The Golden Age lost one
of its smallest stars.

63
00:02:56,393 --> 00:03:00,449
Brad Renfro was discovered
in his Tennessee school at eleven

64
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:04,193
and cast opposite Susan
Sarandon in The Client.

65
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:07,953
The industry called him
a once-in-a-decade natural.

66
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:11,389
But fame arrived faster
than he could carry it,

67
00:03:11,473 --> 00:03:14,133
and addiction followed him into adulthood.

68
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:19,049
He died of a heroin overdose in two
thousand eight at twenty-five.

69
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:21,789
Bobby Driscoll was Disney's golden boy,

70
00:03:21,873 --> 00:03:24,229
the voice and model for Peter Pan,

71
00:03:24,313 --> 00:03:26,209
the boy who never grows up.

72
00:03:26,293 --> 00:03:28,429
But when his adolescent looks faded,

73
00:03:28,513 --> 00:03:30,413
the studio cut him loose.

74
00:03:30,553 --> 00:03:32,289
He drifted into addiction

75
00:03:32,373 --> 00:03:37,189
and died alone in an abandoned New
York tenement in nineteen sixty-eight

76
00:03:37,273 --> 00:03:38,593
at thirty-one.

77
00:03:38,753 --> 00:03:40,993
His body went unidentified.

78
00:03:41,173 --> 00:03:44,673
Peter Pan was buried in an unmarked grave.

79
00:03:45,273 --> 00:03:48,793
Dana Plato was Kimberly
Drummond on Diff'rent Strokes,

80
00:03:48,953 --> 00:03:51,533
one of the most watched
kids on television.

81
00:03:51,813 --> 00:03:52,949
After the show,

82
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:55,793
work dried up and troubles multiplied.

83
00:03:55,933 --> 00:03:57,409
In nineteen ninety-nine,

84
00:03:57,493 --> 00:03:58,709
at thirty-four,

85
00:03:58,793 --> 00:04:02,193
she died of an overdose
that was ruled a suicide

86
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:06,893
the day after a radio interview
where she insisted she was doing fine.

87
00:04:07,913 --> 00:04:08,829
Gary Coleman,

88
00:04:08,913 --> 00:04:09,969
her co-star,

89
00:04:10,053 --> 00:04:12,889
turned, "What you talkin' 'bout, Willis?"

90
00:04:12,973 --> 00:04:15,493
into a permanent piece of pop culture.

91
00:04:15,593 --> 00:04:20,473
A kidney condition stunted his growth
and shadowed his health all his life.

92
00:04:20,573 --> 00:04:22,069
In two thousand and ten,

93
00:04:22,153 --> 00:04:23,769
after a fall at his home,

94
00:04:23,853 --> 00:04:25,593
he died at forty-two,

95
00:04:25,713 --> 00:04:29,213
the third Diff'rent Strokes
child star gone too soon.

96
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:32,633
Corey Haim was half of the two Coreys,

97
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:35,913
the teen idol behind
The Lost Boys and Lucas.

98
00:04:36,133 --> 00:04:38,693
The phone stopped ringing by his twenties,

99
00:04:38,813 --> 00:04:40,933
and pills filled the silence.

100
00:04:41,273 --> 00:04:44,133
He died in two thousand
and ten at thirty-eight,

101
00:04:44,293 --> 00:04:45,973
officially of pneumonia,

102
00:04:46,093 --> 00:04:49,153
after years of addiction
had hollowed out his health.

103
00:04:49,613 --> 00:04:54,473
Heather O'Rourke said the scariest
line in horror history, "They're here."

104
00:04:54,713 --> 00:04:58,669
The little girl from Poltergeist died
suddenly in nineteen eighty-eight.

105
00:04:58,753 --> 00:05:00,049
Cardiac arrest

106
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:04,553
caused by septic shock from an intestinal
defect doctors had missed.

107
00:05:04,733 --> 00:05:06,033
She was twelve.

108
00:05:06,133 --> 00:05:10,773
The franchise's infamous curse
legend was born from losses like hers.

109
00:05:11,513 --> 00:05:14,453
Jonathan Brandis was
everywhere in the nineties.

110
00:05:14,573 --> 00:05:16,273
seaQuest DSV,

111
00:05:16,373 --> 00:05:17,429
Ladybugs,

112
00:05:17,513 --> 00:05:19,433
The NeverEnding Story Two.

113
00:05:19,573 --> 00:05:21,461
When the teen idol years ended,

114
00:05:21,545 --> 00:05:23,145
the roles thinned out.

115
00:05:23,365 --> 00:05:24,901
In two 2003,

116
00:05:24,985 --> 00:05:26,241
at twenty-seven,

117
00:05:26,325 --> 00:05:27,865
he took his own life.

118
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:32,125
Friends said he couldn't accept that the
career he loved was already behind him.

119
00:05:32,385 --> 00:05:35,301
Lee Thompson Young was
the famous Jett Jackson,

120
00:05:35,385 --> 00:05:37,861
Disney's first Black teen action lead,

121
00:05:37,945 --> 00:05:40,845
and later a standout on Rizzoli & Isles.

122
00:05:41,105 --> 00:05:42,701
Behind the steady career,

123
00:05:42,785 --> 00:05:44,845
he battled bipolar disorder.

124
00:05:45,185 --> 00:05:47,481
In 2013, at twenty-nine,

125
00:05:47,565 --> 00:05:49,365
he died by suicide.

126
00:05:49,465 --> 00:05:53,865
His family later created a foundation
to erase the stigma he faced.

127
00:05:54,565 --> 00:05:55,581
Sawyer Sweeten

128
00:05:55,665 --> 00:06:00,625
spent nine seasons on Everybody Loves
Raymond alongside his twin brother,

129
00:06:00,905 --> 00:06:03,001
literally growing up on camera.

130
00:06:03,085 --> 00:06:04,161
The show ended,

131
00:06:04,245 --> 00:06:05,781
normal life began,

132
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:07,581
and it never quite fit.

133
00:06:07,665 --> 00:06:09,081
In 2015,

134
00:06:09,165 --> 00:06:11,601
just weeks before his twentieth birthday,

135
00:06:11,685 --> 00:06:14,725
he died by suicide
at a family member's home.

136
00:06:15,385 --> 00:06:19,865
Skye McCole Bartusiak played Mel
Gibson's daughter in The Patriot,

137
00:06:19,985 --> 00:06:22,061
the little girl who wouldn't speak

138
00:06:22,145 --> 00:06:23,425
until she did.

139
00:06:23,805 --> 00:06:25,861
She kept acting into adulthood,

140
00:06:25,945 --> 00:06:27,581
but in 2014,

141
00:06:27,665 --> 00:06:28,965
at twenty-one,

142
00:06:29,065 --> 00:06:32,961
an accidental combination
of painkillers and muscle relaxants

143
00:06:33,045 --> 00:06:34,945
ended her life in her sleep.

144
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:36,901
Carl Switzer,

145
00:06:36,985 --> 00:06:38,021
Alfalfa,

146
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:40,361
the cow-licked crooner of Our Gang,

147
00:06:40,445 --> 00:06:44,645
grew up to find that Hollywood
had no use for former child stars.

148
00:06:44,965 --> 00:06:46,601
In 1959,

149
00:06:46,685 --> 00:06:49,701
during an argument over
fifty dollars he was owed,

150
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:51,825
an acquaintance shot him dead.

151
00:06:51,985 --> 00:06:53,405
He was thirty-one.

152
00:06:53,605 --> 00:06:56,625
The killer walked free
on a self-defense claim.

153
00:06:57,165 --> 00:07:00,481
Matthew Garber was Michael
Banks in Mary Poppins,

154
00:07:00,565 --> 00:07:02,841
the boy chasing a kite into the sky.

155
00:07:02,925 --> 00:07:07,025
He made three Disney films and then
vanished from screens by choice.

156
00:07:07,185 --> 00:07:08,861
In 1977,

157
00:07:08,945 --> 00:07:11,981
he contracted hepatitis
while traveling in India,

158
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:14,745
and it turned into fatal pancreatitis.

159
00:07:14,845 --> 00:07:16,245
He was twenty-one.

160
00:07:16,845 --> 00:07:21,145
Rob Knox had just filmed Harry
Potter and the Half-Blood Prince,

161
00:07:21,325 --> 00:07:23,645
his big break as Marcus Belby.

162
00:07:23,885 --> 00:07:26,461
Days after wrapping in 2008,

163
00:07:26,545 --> 00:07:29,981
he stepped between a knife-wielding
attacker and his younger brother

164
00:07:30,065 --> 00:07:31,725
outside a London bar.

165
00:07:31,945 --> 00:07:33,225
He was eighteen.

166
00:07:33,425 --> 00:07:37,045
His family turned the loss
into a campaign against knife crime.

167
00:07:37,365 --> 00:07:40,661
Dominique Dunne played
the older sister in Poltergeist,

168
00:07:40,745 --> 00:07:42,785
her first major film role.

169
00:07:42,945 --> 00:07:45,521
Weeks after its 1982 release,

170
00:07:45,605 --> 00:07:48,519
her ex-boyfriend attacked
her outside her home.

171
00:07:48,659 --> 00:07:51,379
She died days later at twenty-two.

172
00:07:51,599 --> 00:07:55,555
The lenient sentence her killer
received outraged the nation

173
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:58,059
and fueled victims' rights reforms.

174
00:07:58,599 --> 00:08:02,115
Rebecca Schaeffer starred
on the sitcom My Sister Sam

175
00:08:02,199 --> 00:08:04,439
and was on the edge of real stardom.

176
00:08:04,799 --> 00:08:06,295
In 1989,

177
00:08:06,379 --> 00:08:09,615
an obsessed fan who had
tracked down her home address

178
00:08:09,699 --> 00:08:11,819
shot her on her own doorstep.

179
00:08:11,979 --> 00:08:13,375
She was twenty-one.

180
00:08:13,459 --> 00:08:18,639
Her death pushed California to pass
America's first anti-stalking laws.

181
00:08:19,479 --> 00:08:23,855
Jonchelle Alexander was twelve when
she lit up Beasts of the Southern Wild,

182
00:08:23,939 --> 00:08:28,715
a Louisiana girl with no acting training
who stole every scene she touched.

183
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:30,559
She never acted again.

184
00:08:30,999 --> 00:08:32,375
In 2022,

185
00:08:32,459 --> 00:08:33,575
at twenty-two,

186
00:08:33,659 --> 00:08:36,719
she was shot while sitting
in a car in New Orleans.

187
00:08:37,359 --> 00:08:40,155
Michelle Trachtenberg was Harriet the Spy,

188
00:08:40,239 --> 00:08:41,959
then Buffy's Little Sister,

189
00:08:42,059 --> 00:08:44,499
then Gossip Girl's Georgina Sparks.

190
00:08:44,679 --> 00:08:47,079
Three eras of kids grew up with her.

191
00:08:47,379 --> 00:08:50,515
After years of health
struggles and a liver transplant,

192
00:08:50,599 --> 00:08:55,219
she died in February 2025
of complications from diabetes.

193
00:08:55,359 --> 00:08:56,859
She was thirty-nine.

194
00:08:57,419 --> 00:09:01,835
Christopher Pettiet rode into living rooms
as a young gunslinger on The Young Riders

195
00:09:01,919 --> 00:09:03,519
in the early '90s.

196
00:09:03,659 --> 00:09:05,575
Like so many on this list,

197
00:09:05,659 --> 00:09:08,879
the transition out of child
stardom proved brutal.

198
00:09:09,059 --> 00:09:10,135
In 2000,

199
00:09:10,219 --> 00:09:11,499
at twenty-four,

200
00:09:11,639 --> 00:09:15,119
he died of an accidental
drug overdose in Los Angeles.

201
00:09:15,739 --> 00:09:18,095
Josh Ryan Evans was three feet two inches

202
00:09:18,179 --> 00:09:22,495
tall and commanded every scene as
Timmy the living doll on Passions

203
00:09:22,579 --> 00:09:25,599
and played the young Grinch
behind all that makeup.

204
00:09:25,699 --> 00:09:29,355
He was born with a heart condition
doctors said would limit his life.

205
00:09:29,439 --> 00:09:30,395
It did.

206
00:09:30,479 --> 00:09:32,579
He died in 2002

207
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:33,859
at twenty

208
00:09:34,039 --> 00:09:38,099
on the exact same day his character's
death aired on television.

209
00:09:38,479 --> 00:09:42,355
Sammy Kane Kraft was a real-
life Little League pitching star

210
00:09:42,439 --> 00:09:46,738
when she was cast in the 2005
remake of The Bad News Bears,

211
00:09:46,979 --> 00:09:49,599
chosen because she could
actually throw heat.

212
00:09:49,879 --> 00:09:51,295
In 2012,

213
00:09:51,379 --> 00:09:52,375
at twenty,

214
00:09:52,459 --> 00:09:57,139
she was killed as a passenger in a car
accident on a Los Angeles freeway.

215
00:09:57,659 --> 00:09:59,299
Ashley Aston Moore

216
00:09:59,479 --> 00:10:01,739
played young Chrissy in Now and Then,

217
00:10:01,959 --> 00:10:05,699
part of the beloved ensemble
that defined '90s girlhood.

218
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:07,815
She left acting as a teenager.

219
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:09,315
In 2007,

220
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:10,675
at 26,

221
00:10:10,759 --> 00:10:13,719
she died of an accidental heroin overdose,

222
00:10:13,819 --> 00:10:16,899
another child of the spotlight
lost far from it.

223
00:10:17,219 --> 00:10:20,370
Justin Pierce was discovered
skateboarding in New York

224
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:24,054
and cast in the raw 1995 film Kids,

225
00:10:24,194 --> 00:10:26,514
then stole scenes in Next Friday.

226
00:10:26,694 --> 00:10:29,214
The fame never settled into stability.

227
00:10:29,514 --> 00:10:30,550
In 2000,

228
00:10:30,634 --> 00:10:31,870
at 25,

229
00:10:31,954 --> 00:10:35,294
he took his own life
in a Las Vegas hotel room.

230
00:10:35,634 --> 00:10:37,330
Nikita Pearl Waligwa

231
00:10:37,414 --> 00:10:40,474
played Gloria in Disney's Queen of Katwe,

232
00:10:40,714 --> 00:10:42,894
the friend who taught the chess champion,

233
00:10:43,054 --> 00:10:44,910
telling her, "In chess,

234
00:10:44,994 --> 00:10:47,234
the small one can become the big one."

235
00:10:47,554 --> 00:10:49,634
She dreamed of becoming a doctor.

236
00:10:49,874 --> 00:10:52,434
A brain tumor took her in 2020.

237
00:10:52,554 --> 00:10:53,954
She was 15.

238
00:10:58,614 --> 00:10:59,970
Milly Inbetween,

239
00:11:00,054 --> 00:11:01,254
almost never.

240
00:11:01,414 --> 00:11:02,750
Bright, funny,

241
00:11:02,834 --> 00:11:04,874
and seemingly unstoppable.

242
00:11:05,154 --> 00:11:06,570
In 2019,

243
00:11:06,654 --> 00:11:07,770
at 16,

244
00:11:07,854 --> 00:11:10,334
she was found unresponsive at home.

245
00:11:10,474 --> 00:11:13,614
A coroner later ruled
her death a misadventure.

246
00:11:13,794 --> 00:11:16,834
Her loss stunned
a generation of young viewers.

247
00:11:17,094 --> 00:11:20,314
Michael Cuccione made people laugh as QT

248
00:11:20,414 --> 00:11:22,454
in the boy band spoof Together,

249
00:11:22,714 --> 00:11:25,190
all while battling Hodgkin's lymphoma,

250
00:11:25,274 --> 00:11:27,314
which he'd survived as a child.

251
00:11:27,634 --> 00:11:30,894
He used his fame to raise
money for cancer research,

252
00:11:31,014 --> 00:11:33,354
even writing songs for the cause.

253
00:11:33,694 --> 00:11:38,234
The disease's complications
took him in 2001 at 16.

254
00:11:38,574 --> 00:11:40,530
Anissa Jones was Buffy

255
00:11:40,614 --> 00:11:42,094
on Family Affair,

256
00:11:42,254 --> 00:11:43,590
pigtails and Mrs.

257
00:11:43,674 --> 00:11:44,874
Beasley doll,

258
00:11:45,074 --> 00:11:47,894
one of the biggest
child stars of the '70s.

259
00:11:48,174 --> 00:11:53,654
But she was typecast so completely that
no one would hire the teenager she became.

260
00:11:54,134 --> 00:11:55,970
In 1976,

261
00:11:56,054 --> 00:11:57,250
at 18,

262
00:11:57,334 --> 00:11:59,994
she died of a massive drug overdose.

263
00:12:00,274 --> 00:12:01,650
Bridgette Anderson

264
00:12:01,734 --> 00:12:04,690
was the runaway sweetheart
of Savannah Smiles,

265
00:12:04,774 --> 00:12:07,534
a performance film critics still praise.

266
00:12:07,734 --> 00:12:09,690
Adult life was unkind.

267
00:12:09,774 --> 00:12:12,494
Addiction took hold and never let go.

268
00:12:12,614 --> 00:12:18,094
She died of an accidental
overdose in 1997 at 21.

269
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:22,494
Rusty Hamer grew up for 11
seasons on Make Room for Daddy,

270
00:12:22,674 --> 00:12:25,594
Danny Thomas' wise-cracking TV son.

271
00:12:25,694 --> 00:12:27,210
When the cameras stopped,

272
00:12:27,294 --> 00:12:29,294
the work never really came back.

273
00:12:29,394 --> 00:12:30,730
In 1990,

274
00:12:30,814 --> 00:12:31,970
at 42,

275
00:12:32,054 --> 00:12:33,810
he died by suicide,

276
00:12:33,894 --> 00:12:38,714
a loss that helped inspire Paul Peterson's
advocacy for former child actors.

277
00:12:39,414 --> 00:12:42,894
Logan Williams played the young
Barry Allen on The Flash,

278
00:12:42,994 --> 00:12:45,150
the kid version of a superhero.

279
00:12:45,234 --> 00:12:46,430
In 2020,

280
00:12:46,514 --> 00:12:47,669
at sixteen,

281
00:12:47,753 --> 00:12:50,033
he died of a fentanyl overdose.

282
00:12:50,213 --> 00:12:52,849
His mother spoke publicly
about his struggle,

283
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:56,053
hoping honesty might
save someone else's child.

284
00:12:56,633 --> 00:13:00,489
Tyler Sanders starred in Just
Add Magic, Mystery City,

285
00:13:00,573 --> 00:13:03,793
and shared scenes in 9-1-1 Lone Star,

286
00:13:04,053 --> 00:13:06,653
earning an Emmy nomination as a teenager.

287
00:13:07,073 --> 00:13:08,369
In twenty twenty-two,

288
00:13:08,453 --> 00:13:09,569
at eighteen,

289
00:13:09,653 --> 00:13:11,973
he died from the effects of fentanyl,

290
00:13:12,253 --> 00:13:14,409
part of a counterfeit pill crisis

291
00:13:14,493 --> 00:13:17,233
now claiming young lives across America.

292
00:13:17,653 --> 00:13:19,213
Thirty-five names.

293
00:13:19,453 --> 00:13:21,773
Thirty-five unfinished stories.

294
00:13:22,173 --> 00:13:25,053
And here's what stays with you
after hearing them all.

295
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,393
Some were taken by illness,

296
00:13:27,493 --> 00:13:28,933
some by violence,

297
00:13:29,053 --> 00:13:31,713
some by accidents no one could see coming,

298
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:33,489
and far too many

299
00:13:33,573 --> 00:13:36,049
by a machine that celebrates children

300
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:38,969
and then forgets them
the moment the ratings move on.

301
00:13:39,053 --> 00:13:41,793
Laws changed because of Rebecca Schaeffer.

302
00:13:42,033 --> 00:13:45,209
Foundations exist
because of Cameron Boyce,

303
00:13:45,293 --> 00:13:46,749
Lee Thompson Young,

304
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:47,849
Rob Knox,

305
00:13:47,933 --> 00:13:49,649
and Michael Cuccione.

306
00:13:49,733 --> 00:13:51,609
Their stories did not end.

307
00:13:51,693 --> 00:13:54,273
They were handed
to the rest of us to carry.

308
00:13:54,673 --> 00:13:57,573
So the real question isn't
how many you remembered,

309
00:13:57,673 --> 00:13:59,733
it's how many you'll remember now.

310
00:14:00,053 --> 00:14:02,229
If this video meant something to you,

311
00:14:02,313 --> 00:14:04,989
share the name that stayed
with you in the comments

312
00:14:05,073 --> 00:14:06,349
and subscribe

313
00:14:06,433 --> 00:14:11,049
because every one of these young stars
deserves to be more than a headline.

314
00:14:11,133 --> 00:14:12,973
They deserve to be remembered

